# WS-D2 — Codex adversarial-critic leg + calibration (adversarial-review amendment)

Per `docs/plans/ws-d2-codex-critic-leg.md`. Adds the Codex critic leg to the
SEALED adversarial-review component as the WS-D1 model-role registry's FIRST
non-default entry — a second critic on a DIFFERENT model family (OpenAI
Codex) running in PARALLEL with the default Claude critic (author=Claude /
adversary=Codex; error de-correlation across families, the objective's
`model-rationale`).

New `codex.py`, all additive:

  - AC.CDX.1 (outcome-altitude) — n=1 calibration: a seeded-flaw artifact run
    through the Codex leg via the production pipeline (`calibrate(...
    registry=codex_critic_registry(include_claude=False))` and `review_text`)
    surfaces the planted defect, tagged `leg="codex"`, and `calibrate` reads
    back a nonzero catch rate. Deterministic, mirroring the sealed AC.AR.10
    posture: only the `codex` process boundary (`shutil.which` +
    `subprocess.run`) is stubbed — the real argv-build, env-scrub, `--json`
    extraction, `parse_findings`, registry resolution, and calibration
    scoring all execute. `run_codex_critic` is a plain text `ModelFn` routed
    through the UNCHANGED two-phase `run_critic` (D-CDX.1: reuse the sealed
    critic primitive, no parallel single-phase codex pass).
  - AC.CDX.2 — with `codex` uninstalled (`shutil.which` -> None, the REAL
    fail-soft path), a review whose CRITIC role is `(claude, codex)`
    completes on the claude leg and NAMES the missing `codex` leg
    (`missing_legs == ("codex",)`, surfaced in `render_report`); never an
    unmarked clean bill. All legs down -> REVIEW INCONCLUSIVE (the existing
    floor), never a false PASS.
  - AC.CDX.3 — the leg's subprocess env (the `env=` handed to
    `subprocess.run`) carries no `OPENAI_API_KEY` and no `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`
    under D2's ChatGPT-sign-in auth, while `HOME`/`PATH` survive (sign-in is
    file-based). Scrub is by DELETION over `os.environ`, not a minimal
    whitelist (D-CDX.3). An `allow_openai_key=True` escape hatch relaxes the
    `OPENAI_API_KEY` scrub for THIS subprocess only (D2's metered-key clause),
    never globally; default is sign-in-only.

Named method decisions (builder's call per ODD §1.1, recorded in the plan):
D-CDX.2 DROPS the plan hint's `--output-schema` (a fixed findings schema is
incompatible with the two-phase `ModelFn` reuse — DERIVE must emit a
free-form spec; no AC binds the schema and the downstream `FINDING…END`
regex is format-agnostic); `--sandbox read-only` is KEPT and required (a
critic reads, never mutates). D-CDX.4 keeps the leg a LIBRARY factory
(`codex_critic_registry` + the existing `registry=` param), NOT a new CLI
flag — an unnamed CLI branch would be non-objective code. D-CDX.5: the
live-codex model-quality proof is owner-gated (codex not installed at build;
the plan's own dependency line gates install + D2 sign-in on the owner) and
ships as the opt-in `test_AR_S_real_codex_smoke` (`AR_REAL_CODEX=1`,
auto-skipped when codex absent) — the exact posture the sealed component
already uses for its live calibration smoke; NOT an AC downgrade (wiring,
tagging, fail-soft, and env-scrub are all verified through the production
pipeline).

`calibration.calibrate` gains an additive `registry` kwarg threaded to
`review_text` (default None ⇒ unchanged). The sealed default single-Claude
path is byte-identical: `render_report`, `critic.py`, `registry.py`,
`pipeline.py`, `manual.py`, `gate.py`, `spawn.py` are UNCHANGED, and the full
AC.AR.{1-13}+AC.MRR.{1-3}+AR.S suite passes unmodified. The sealed
loam-spawn-isolation surface is NOT imported — codex is a different binary
spawned directly, reaching nothing sealed (the dispatch's probe_liveness /
sys.path-reuse note is fleet/lease boilerplate, inapplicable here).
`.claude/settings.json` (Track F single-writer) is UNTOUCHED — no hook.

